Z||000001||Xtreme Fiero's||10-21-2000||11:25 AM||||Fiero TT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I would love a twin turbo fiero. BUT would you set it up like say a TT Supra & RX-7 or like a 3000GT or 300ZX the system I have on my Truck is from a 300ZX and runs two Garrett T-2 turbos though it no complete yet (if ever) they will run at the same time for very good performance. but the systems on RX-7's & Supra TT's use a LARGE turbo & a small turbo the car would make boost of the small one until aroun 3000rpm and "Change over" to the larger one. thus keeping lag down and the car streetable.<P> on a fiero I would wait until Chris West get his dual TB inake done and give each TB a fair sized turbo. and get a good exaust shop to make a custom Y-pipe.<P>Somebody may know better than me on this one For boost control and a blow-off valve could you cut a hole in the center of the decklid and machine the upper manifold ot mout a blow-off valve there. It worked on my 84' SE BUT it was still before the TBI unit. does it have to be before the Thrttle plates? if so (I think is does) good luck fiting two in there.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||13
